WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:16.201
Mr. Brownlow's home, Oliver was immediately put to bed.

2
00:00:17.161 --> 00:00:21.764
Mr. Brownlow's housekeeper sat by the bed, patiently waiting for Oliver to recover from his fever.

3
00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:26.367
But for many days, he remained insensible to the goodness of his new friends.

4
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:30.450
At last he awoke from what seemed to be a long, troubled dream.

5
00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.125
Feebly raising his head, he said, "Where am I?"

6
00:00:34.145 --> 00:00:37.027
"Hush, my dear," said Mrs.

7
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.388
Bedwin, the old housekeeper.

8
00:00:38.408 --> 00:00:41.451
"You must be quiet or you'll be ill again.

9
00:00:42.552 --> 00:00:43.172
Lie down."

10
00:00:44.173 --> 00:00:46.835
With that, she gently smoothed his hair back from his face.

11
00:00:47.936 --> 00:00:50.318
She looked so kind that he put his hand in hers.

12
00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:53.561
"What a grateful little dear," said Mrs.

13
00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.082
Bedwin with tears in her eyes.

14
00:00:55.102 --> 00:00:58.505
"What would his mother think if she could see him now?"

15
00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.768
"Perhaps she does see me," whispered Oliver.

16
00:01:03.516 --> 00:01:05.138
"I feel as if she's been here with me."

17
00:01:05.158 --> 00:01:07.520
"That was the fever, dear."

18
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.723
"I suppose it was," said Oliver after a moment's silence.

19
00:01:11.743 --> 00:01:15.326
"If she'd seen me ill, it would have made her sad.

20
00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:18.830
Her face always looks so happy when I dream of her."

21
00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.253
Mrs. Bedwin brought Oliver something cool to drink and he fell asleep again.

22
00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:28.198
It was another three days before the fever passed and Oliver was able to sit up.

23
00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:31.381
He was still too weak to walk, so Mrs.

24
00:01:31.421 --> 00:01:34.063
Bedwin had him carried downstairs to her own little room.

25
00:01:35.104 --> 00:01:38.207
Propped up with pillows, he sat in a chair next to the fire while Mrs.

26
00:01:38.247 --> 00:01:39.768
Bedwin warmed some broth for him.

27
00:01:39.788 --> 00:01:42.130
"Are you fond of pictures?"

28
00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.031
asked Mrs.

29
00:01:43.091 --> 00:01:45.633
Bedwin, who noticed him studying a portrait on the wall.

30
00:01:45.653 --> 00:01:47.795
"I don't quite know, ma'am.

31
00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.777
I've seen so few of them.

32
00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.660
What a beautiful face that lady has.

33
00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:55.401
Who is she?"

34
00:01:55.421 --> 00:01:58.024
"I have no idea, my dear."

35
00:01:59.092 --> 00:02:01.274
Mrs. Bedwin handed Oliver a bowl of broth.

36
00:02:02.314 --> 00:02:05.076
To him it seemed rich enough to feed a room full of paupers.

37
00:02:06.157 --> 00:02:08.839
He continued to stare at the portrait while he sipped his broth.

38
00:02:08.859 --> 00:02:12.501
"It looks as if she wants to speak to me," he said.

39
00:02:13.522 --> 00:02:17.885
Oliver had scarcely swallowed his last bit of broth when there was a knock at the door, and

40
00:02:18.005 --> 00:02:18.705
in walked Mr.

41
00:02:18.725 --> 00:02:23.128
Brownlow. Oliver tried to stand up as a mark of respect for his benefactor.

42
00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:26.551
But he was too weak and sank back into his chair.

43
00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:28.212
"Poor boy!"

44
00:02:28.616 --> 00:02:29.016
said Mr.

45
00:02:29.057 --> 00:02:31.538
Brownlow. "How do you feel, my dear?"

46
00:02:31.558 --> 00:02:33.440
"Very happy, sir.

47
00:02:34.421 --> 00:02:36.722
And very grateful indeed for your goodness toward me."

48
00:02:36.742 --> 00:02:39.745
"I'm glad to hear that, Tom White."

49
00:02:40.766 --> 00:02:42.707
"My name is Oliver Twist, sir."

50
00:02:43.708 --> 00:02:44.929
Mr. Brownlow looked puzzled.

51
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:48.392
"But why did you tell the magistrate your name was Tom White?"

52
00:02:48.412 --> 00:02:50.213
"I didn't, sir."

53
00:02:51.214 --> 00:02:53.956
Mr. Brownlow studied Oliver's face to see if he was lying.

54
00:02:54.888 --> 00:02:58.551
And once again he felt strongly that there was something familiar about Oliver.

55
00:02:58.571 --> 00:03:00.993
"You're not angry with me, sir?"

56
00:03:01.353 --> 00:03:01.934
asked Oliver.

57
00:03:01.954 --> 00:03:04.596
"No, no said Mr.

58
00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:05.617
Brownlow distractedly.

59
00:03:05.637 --> 00:03:07.078
"Look, Mrs.

60
00:03:07.118 --> 00:03:08.019
Bedwin, look there!"

61
00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.921
He pointed at the portrait and then to Oliver.

62
00:03:11.842 --> 00:03:14.644
There was no missing the resemblance between the lady and the boy.

63
00:03:15.685 --> 00:03:20.189
Oliver suddenly felt weak, and as the two adults stared at him, he lost consciousness.

64
00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:25.965
Meanwhile, as soon as Oliver had been captured by the police, Charley Bates and the Artful Dodger ran

65
00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:26.425
for home.

66
00:03:26.445 --> 00:03:28.967
"Where's Oliver?"

67
00:03:29.287 --> 00:03:30.608
thundered Fagin when they arrived.

68
00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.850
The two boys looked at each other but said nothing.

69
00:03:34.891 --> 00:03:38.553
Fagin grabbed the Dodger by the collar of his huge coat and began shaking him.

70
00:03:38.573 --> 00:03:40.374
"The police have him.

71
00:03:41.394 --> 00:03:43.616
That's all there is to the story," said the Dodger.

72
00:03:43.636 --> 00:03:45.317
"Let go of me."

73
00:03:46.317 --> 00:03:50.240
And with one jerk, he swung himself out of the coat, which he left in Fagin's hand.

74
00:03:51.316 --> 00:03:54.617
He snatched up a toasting fork and poked it at the old man's waistcoat.

75
00:03:54.637 --> 00:03:56.938
"Hey!" cried a new voice.

76
00:03:56.958 --> 00:03:58.999
"What's going on here?"

77
00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:03.901
A stoutly built fellow entered the room, accompanied by a shaggy white dog.

78
00:04:03.921 --> 00:04:06.102
"What are you up to, Fagin?

79
00:04:07.103 --> 00:04:09.203
Maltreating the boys, you covetous old crook?

80
00:04:10.184 --> 00:04:11.884
It's a wonder the boys don't murder you.

81
00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.306
That's what I'd have done if I were your apprentice, helping you fence stolen goods."

82
00:04:18.247 --> 00:04:18.907
"Hush, Mr.

83
00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:20.308
Sikes," said Fagin.

84
00:04:21.356 --> 00:04:22.736
"Don't speak so loudly."

85
00:04:22.756 --> 00:04:26.298
"You always mean mischief when you call me Mister Sikes."

86
00:04:26.318 --> 00:04:31.219
"Well then, Bill Sikes," said Fagin, anxious to please.

87
00:04:31.239 --> 00:04:33.200
"Would you like a drink?"

88
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.640
"Make sure you don't poison it."

89
00:04:36.781 --> 00:04:40.802
Sikes said this in jest, but Fagin gave an evil leer as he poured out the drink.

90
00:04:41.922 --> 00:04:45.163
After swallowing two or three drinks, Sikes looked at the boys again.

91
00:04:46.183 --> 00:04:48.104
This led to a conversation about Oliver.

92
00:04:49.108 --> 00:04:52.229
"I'm afraid he'll say something that'll get us into trouble," said Fagin.

93
00:04:52.249 --> 00:04:57.350
"And things might come out even worse for you since you're in the business of robbing houses."

94
00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.491
"We have to find out what happened at the police station," said Sikes.

95
00:05:01.511 --> 00:05:04.212
"You have to get hold of this boy somehow."

96
00:05:05.993 --> 00:05:10.334
Fagin nodded in agreement, but no one in the room wanted to go anywhere near the police station.

97
00:05:11.314 --> 00:05:13.775
Fortunately for them, Nancy arrived just then.

98
00:05:13.795 --> 00:05:17.416
"Nancy will go to the police station, won't you, my dear?"

99
00:05:17.776 --> 00:05:18.356
said Fagin.

100
00:05:19.492 --> 00:05:21.053
"She'll go," said Sikes.

101
00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:24.475
"No, she won't, Fagin," said Nancy.

102
00:05:24.495 --> 00:05:27.957
"Yes, she will, Fagin," said Sikes.

103
00:05:29.098 --> 00:05:30.118
And Sikes was right.

104
00:05:31.059 --> 00:05:34.481
By alternately threatening and bribing her, the men forced Nancy to go.

105
00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:39.143
"Wait a minute, my dear," said Fagin as Nancy was preparing to leave.

106
00:05:40.244 --> 00:05:43.426
He tied a white apron around her waist and gave her a covered basket.

107
00:05:43.446 --> 00:05:47.388
"Carry that in one hand; it looks more respectable."

108
00:05:48.408 --> 00:05:49.749
"Oh, my poor little brother!"

109
00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:52.790
Nancy exclaimed as she burst into tears.

110
00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.192
"What has become of him?"

111
00:05:56.252 --> 00:05:58.714
Nancy winked at the men and disappeared out the door.

112
00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:02.756
"Ah, she's a clever one," said Fagin.

113
00:06:03.836 --> 00:06:07.158
Nancy arrived at the police station and went from one cell door to another.

114
00:06:08.179 --> 00:06:12.621
But Oliver wasn't in any of the cells, so she was forced to talk to a police officer.

115
00:06:12.641 --> 00:06:14.682
"Have you seen my brother?"

116
00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:15.583
she asked.

117
00:06:16.623 --> 00:06:18.024
"He's a sweet-faced little dear."

118
00:06:19.084 --> 00:06:21.145
"The gentleman took him," explained the policeman.

119
00:06:22.246 --> 00:06:26.368
Nancy obtained a few more details about Oliver's release and then ran back to Fagin's.

120
00:06:26.388 --> 00:06:28.609
"We must find him!"

121
00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.530
said Fagin.

122
00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.651
"Charley! Nancy!

123
00:06:31.931 --> 00:06:35.453
Dodger! Do nothing but skulk about until you find him.

124
00:06:36.474 --> 00:06:37.694
I'll shut up this place tonight.

125
00:06:38.775 --> 00:06:39.836
You'll know where to find me."

126
00:06:40.856 --> 00:06:42.717
With that, he pushed them out the door.

127
00:06:43.718 --> 00:06:47.380
Then he barred the door and pulled from its hiding place the box that Oliver had seen.

128
00:06:48.416 --> 00:06:52.984
He quickly hid the watches and jewelry underneath his clothing and went out into the city.
